- How would you extend to prioritize certain domains or implement exponential backoff on failures?

## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests practical control of performance budgets at runtime, tying Lighthouse-like goals to per-route bundling and lazy-loading decisions in production.

## Key Concepts

- Per-route budgets and dynamic import gating
- PerformanceObserver traces for TTI, LCP, long tasks
- Resource hints (preload/prefetch) and idle-time loading
- CI Lighthouse integration and field data correlation

## Code Example

```javascript
// budget gate per route
const ROUTE_BUDGETS = { home: 280000, dashboard: 320000 };
let usedByRoute = {};
function safeLoad(route, path, sizeEstimate) {
  const budget = ROUTE_BUDGETS[route] ?? 300000;
  const used = usedByRoute[route] || 0;
  if (used + sizeEstimate > budget) {
    return import(`./${path}.lite.js`);
  }
  usedByRoute[route] = used + sizeEstimate;
  return import(`./${path}.js`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test budget adherence in CI and in production?
- What metrics would you surface for engineers to tune budgets without breaking UX?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world CSS skills: grid complexity, responsive layouts, animation, and accessibility.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid responsive layouts
- Centered featured element via grid-column/grid-row
- Hover lift plus reduced-motion
- Keyboard navigation in a grid

## Code Example
```javascript
document.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach((el, idx, arr) => {
  el.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    const cols = 4;
    const delta = {ArrowLeft:-1, ArrowRight:1, ArrowUp:-cols, ArrowDown:cols}[e.key];
    if (delta !== undefined) {
      const next = arr[(idx + delta + arr.length) % arr.length];
      next.focus();
    }
  });
  el.setAttribute('tabindex','0');
});
```

